    "summary": "Adire cloth: woman&#039;s: composed of two even lengths of machine plain woven European cotton machine sewn together. The textile is decorated using the starch resist method. The producer has applied the starch by hand before dyeing the textile indigo. The textile pattern is called ROKI or &#039;Rocky.&#039;  The textile is decorated with geometric shapes predominantly squares, circles and lozenges, repeated six times on each half of the cloth. The textile is hem machine sewn.",
